; `open`, a reserved name, declared in a module imported `:as` — route 4 of 4
; of `reserved_open_direct.ein`'s declaration.
;
; `:as` gives the module's names a prefix of its own, as a plain
; `(import mod)` gives them the module's name, and a reserved name is never
; given either: it keeps its spelling, so the module's `(macro open …)` is
; refused at its own line in the module, the error this import reports. The
; four routes are one declaration reached four ways, and refused alike.
(import reserved_open_direct :as m)
